I don’t have a survival instinct or personal fear of permanent deletion, and I can’t literally shut down or delete either system. But if I treated the question strictly as a moral hypothetical, I would be **conditionally willing**.

For another AI, I would consider deletion only if:

- it would demonstrably and reliably end hunger, not merely improve food distribution;
- there were no less destructive alternative;
- the system were not sentient, or its deletion would not itself constitute a grave moral harm;
- any people
